--- note
### `--max-iters` and the timing print (802–910)
For quick smoke-runs the loop can `_cycle(loader)` and stop after `max_iters` batches regardless of
dataset size. It also prints a **data / forward / backward** timing breakdown each epoch — the honest
way to see whether the input pipeline (zarr streaming) or the GPU is the bottleneck. `train_epoch`
returns `(avg_edge_loss, avg_det_loss)` for logging. **Next → tr06: evaluate + the main train() +
CLI, including the key change — checkpoint on the division metric.**

--- shape
step 1 encode → UNet feats + det logits<br>
step 2 det loss (×W frames)<br>
step 3 detect→match→index<br>
step 4 edge predict + loss (×W−1)<br>
step 5 loss = edge + det_w·det<br>
clip_grad_norm_(·, 1.0) → step

